      "writtenOn": "2022-08-24T18:47:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This test should assume that the host command succeeds and has a correctly formatted response. To the extent that this test requires those things to be true, it should use `zassume` instead of `zassert`.\n\nThere should be another test in `zephyr/test/drivers/default/src/espi.c` that actually `zassert`s on the basic function of this host command. The other tests in that file are examples of how to write that kind of test.\n\nIt might also be convenient to put a helper function for calling this host command in `zephyr/test/drivers/common/src/utils.c`.\n\nThat extra stuff can go in another CL if you want.",
      "revId": "1fd0b484ee40c61701641d56059dfc64c57afade",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
